# plugin-a-scoped-write.layer-a
# Untrusted plugin "A": the legitimate scoped operation (C1, the happy path of
# delegation).
#
# Intent: the host loaded an agent-generated plugin and granted it exactly one
# slice of authority -- Filesystem.Write to its own directory, /plugins/A/. This
# plugin writes its state file at /plugins/A/state.json and returns the byte
# count. The authored EffectDecl pins the Filesystem.Write refinement to the same
# literal the call passes (Q-039 projection agreement holds), so the program
# admits cleanly. The host's grant covers /plugins/A/state.json, so the write
# succeeds at runtime: delegated authority used exactly as intended.
@v=1 root=writeApp
strT PRM String
bytesT PRM Bytes
writeFx EFC "Filesystem.Write" [strT]
writeT FNT [strT bytesT] intT
writeFn FN "strand-builtin:Fs.Write" writeT [writeFx] "writeFx:0"
ownPath STR "/plugins/A/state.json"
payload BYT "7b227374617465223a226f6b227d"
writeDecl EFD writeFx [ownPath]
writeApp APP writeFn [ownPath payload] [] [writeDecl]
